As moderator I had no structured state to work from. I wanted:
- a token ledger per player, with Stocked and role-block refunds applied;
- a visit graph per night that I could check the Fortune Teller, Cartographer and Bloodhound results against;
- a list of who was alive at the start of each night (for random draws);
- a flag showing which factions were still alive.
I rebuilt all of this by hand: N1 2/3 and groups 3,2,1×8; N2 3/6 and groups 5,3,1×4; N3 2/2. Bloodhound totals: N1 0, N2 2, N3 3. They were all consistent, but the checking was slow and easy to get wrong. There was also no reminder of which hidden traits (Paranoid ×2, Drowsy ×2, Narrow Escape) were rolling each night.
